> **Why gathered.** Live evidence for the identity/`[slug]` accessor demand (greppable first-line
> citation), for relation-edge modeling inside a document (`|rel :to :kind`), and for the `!:md:`
> raw-dialect escape hatch — including the explicit footgun note that a bare table row parses as an
> element. Head only (schema + §1 opening); the remaining ~565 lines are more `|term` entries in the
> same shape across frozen sections §1–§8.

|lexicon[vivarium] :seeded 2026-07-03 :restructured 2026-07-11 :status living
  :title vivarium — LEXICON (the bounded, ubiquitous vocabulary)

  ; Converted from ad-hoc markdown bullets to dictionary-grade |term entries
  ; 2026-07-11 (Joseph's ask: the headword being adopted must be unmistakable;
  ; definition -> relationships -> boundaries, per term). Section numbers §1-§8
  ; are frozen — external docs cite "LEXICON §5" etc. Prior form: git history.

  |meta[entry-schema]
    :authority PROCESS.udon self-governance valve

    One term per |term element — the [slug] and :name are the headword; what we are adopting is never buried in a compound label. Body: the FIRST paragraph is the definition. Then only-if-real children (a field that is not real is omitted):
    - |not        — what it is not / what not to call it
    - |confused   — easily confused with (and how to tell apart)
    - |rel        — relation edges (:to term-slug :kind verb) — these build the vocabulary graph; keep verbs plain (runs, composes-into, floor-of, occupies, edge-of, ...)
    - |context    — binding scope beyond vivarium/archema; register notes
    - |source     — the design doc carrying the full machinery
    LEXICON states PRESENT TRUTH ONLY. History — what a term replaced, or the collision it was carved against — does NOT live here: it lives in .archive/SUPERSEDED.md, the graveyard index ("do not use this anymore, use that"). |not and |confused stay because they are present-tense disambiguation against a LIVE neighbour, not history. (The |carve field is retired; its 10 blocks moved to the ledger 2026-07-13. One survives, in |term[lineage-head-pinned-regula], frozen pending Joseph's regula-naming call.)
    Statuses (:status): settled (in live use, collision-checked) · carved (chosen against a recorded collision — the collision is recorded in SUPERSEDED.md) · open (needs Joseph's decision; candidates loosely held). Markdown tables live in !:md: blocks (a bare table row would parse as an element). Math stays $...$ LaTeX.

    Why a lexicon at all: (1) carves away from colliding usage must be recorded or future sessions re-collide; (2) project-unique terms carry design decisions inside them, and vague usage quietly un-decides them. The deeper motivation (Joseph, 2026-07-03): the tension web of caching × deterministic seeding × world-building × saves × strictly-causal runs × iteration already produced slowdowns and re-arguing. Names are how we stop re-arguing. A term earns its place by standalone citability ([[naming-principles]]).

    Register convention (2026-07-11, deliberate): Greek = the law-article machinery (nomos family) · Latin = the world-governance layer (regula, regnum, ordinum) · plain English = the lived concepts (Kingdom, Charge, Promise, Record, slot, permit). Register signals layer; a proposal that crosses registers should notice it is doing so.

  ; ==========================================================================
  |section[world-structure] :num 1
    :name World-structure (phases & gates)

    |term[phase] :status carved
      A span in which a set of macro systems runs until converged.
      |rel :to charge :kind must-deliver
      |rel :to promise :kind hands-forward
      |rel :to phase-gate :kind bounded-by
      |source tabularium/terrestris.ordinum.udon

    |term[epoch] :status settled
      Reserved exclusively for the erosion solver's step unit.
      |not a span of world-history (that is a phase); not a geological epoch.

    |term[phase-gate] :status settled :since 2026-07-04
      The boundary between phases — the threshold where the previous phase's Charge is checked and met.
      |rel :to charge :kind opened-by

    |term[phase-transition] :status settled :since 2026-07-04
      The regime-change EVENT at a phase-gate. Incremental, never a wholesale swap: most systems perpetuate, a few sunset, a larger group of new and finer-scale systems spins up at the gate (.archive/PHASES.md Design notes). It leaves the largest memo, and it promotes converged state into Law.
      |rel :to law :kind revises
      |rel :to memo :kind leaves
      |rel :to ordinum :kind floor-checked-against

    |term[charge] :status settled
      What a phase must establish — the GATING SUBSET of its promises. A phase's charge IS the next phase-gate's opening condition.
      |rel :to promise :kind gating-subset-of

; […head extract ends at line 52 of 617 — |term entries continue across frozen sections §1–§8…]
